{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.T211IdealAnnihilation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.T211IdealAnnihilation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.OrderOfElement","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_in_ideal_all_levels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_in_ideal_all_levels","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L191-L195","doc":"T_{2,11} is in the spectral ideal at every brane level.\nThe genus depends only on the winding number p, not the level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.non_embeddable_eigenvalues_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.non_embeddable_eigenvalues_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L170-L185","doc":"The knot operator F(T_{m,n}, N) = 1 for non-embeddable torus knots.\nThe transfer matrix has eigenvalues (1, 1), giving degenerate\nChebyshev recurrence with no shell structure.\n\nThe transfer matrix eigenvalues for a non-embeddable knot are both 1.\nFormally: λ₊(T_{m,n}) = 1 ∧ λ₋(T_{m,n}) = 1.\nThe consequence V̂(k) = 1^k = 1 is proved above (trivial_eigenvalue_flat).\nFull statement requires the transfer matrix type from\nspectral-decomposition-qvalue; the eigenvalue = 1 claim is the\ncontent of embeddability-closure Theorem 2 (spectral filter). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.trivial_eigenvalue_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.trivial_eigenvalue_flat","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L164-L168","doc":"The trivial eigenvalue equation: 1^k = 1 for all k.\nThis is the Chebyshev recurrence at eigenvalues (1,1):\nV̂(n) = 1 for all n — no shell structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_not_embeddable'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_not_embeddable'","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L159-L162","doc":"T_{2,11} does not embed on Σ₄. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.notEmbeddable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.notEmbeddable","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L155-L157","doc":"Non-embeddability condition for T_{m,n} on Σ_g. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.z5_in_s5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.z5_in_s5","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L144-L149","doc":"Z₅ embeds in S₅ via the 5-cycle (0 1 2 3 4): it has prime order 5\n(`theCycle5 ^ 5 = 1` and `theCycle5 ≠ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.z3_in_s5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.z3_in_s5","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L138-L142","doc":"Z₃ embeds in S₅ via the 3-cycle (0 1 2): it has prime order 3\n(`theCycle3 ^ 3 = 1` and `theCycle3 ≠ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.z11_not_in_s5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.z11_not_in_s5","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L113-L120","doc":"Z₁₁ cannot embed in S₅: no element of S₅ has order 11,\nbecause 11 ∤ 120. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.orderOf_perm_dvd_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.orderOf_perm_dvd_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L97-L111","doc":"The order of any element of a finite group divides the group order.\nFor S_n, |S_n| = n!, so orderOf σ ∣ n!.\n\n**Proof**: from Mathlib's `orderOf_dvd_card` (Lagrange) combined\nwith `Fintype.card_perm` (which gives `|Perm (Fin n)| = n!`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eleven_not_dvd_factorial_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eleven_not_dvd_factorial_5","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L93-L95","doc":"11 does not divide 5! = 120. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dihedral_vs_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dihedral_vs_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L84-L87","doc":"D₁₁ is much smaller than S₁₁. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_symmetry_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_symmetry_order","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L80-L82","doc":"|D₁₁| = 22. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dihedralOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dihedralOrder","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L76-L78","doc":"Order of the dihedral group D_p = Z_p ⋊ Z_2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_is_first_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_is_first_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L67-L70","doc":"T_{2,11} is the first excluded: T_{2,9} fits, T_{2,11} does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t2_9_saturates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t2_9_saturates","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L63-L65","doc":"T_{2,9} saturates genus 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_not_embeddable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_not_embeddable","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L59-L61","doc":"T_{2,11} does not embed in genus 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t2_11_genus","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L55-L57","doc":"Seifert genus of T_{2,11} is 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.seifertGenus_T2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.seifertGenus_T2","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L51-L53","doc":"Seifert genus of T_{2,p} is (p-1)/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L44-L45","doc":"The inverse indeterminate `q⁻¹` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_param","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L41-L42","doc":"The canonical indeterminate `q` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.R_q","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/t211-ideal-annihilation.lean#L37-L39","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}